<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Crema</h1><p class="st-meta">1797 CE – 1797 CE · capital Crema</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A brief Jacobin republic proclaimed in Crema in March 1797, when the town broke from Venice in the last weeks of the Serenissima.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crema">Crema</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> town between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-milan">Milan</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-cremona">Cremona</a>, had belonged to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-venice">Republic of Venice</a> since 1449. On 28 March 1797, following the revolts of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-bergamo">Bergamo</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-brescia">Brescia</a> and with French troops present, local patriots deposed the Venetian governor and proclaimed the Cremasque Republic.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic was a provisional government of local notables and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacobin-club">Jacobins</a> under French protection. It abolished Venetian institutions and noble privileges, set up committees on the French model and looked to union with the new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> republics. Little is known of its brief administration.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> in May 1797, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crema">Crema</a> was absorbed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cisalpine-republic">Cisalpine Republic</a> later that year, ending its separate existence.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/republic-of-crema.jpg" alt="Republic of Crema" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Samhanin · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Repubblica_Cremasca.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1797 CE – 1797 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Crema</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Lombard, Italian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Cremasque Republic</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1797&amp;focus=republic-of-crema" aria-label="Republic of Crema on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4910 577 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of Crema lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5230 833L5293 831M5230 833L5218 830"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5293 831h0M5218 830h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5230 833h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5230 833h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Crema. <a href="/atlas?year=1797&amp;focus=republic-of-crema">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
